  "id": "COMPOUND:29896 - PROTEIN:1954",
  "verbalization": "Sinocalycanchinensin G appears to have multiple targets, including Ephrin type-A receptors and 2-keto-3-deoxy-gluconate kinase, which in turn are targets of methohexital. These pathways converge on Protein-L-isoaspartate O-methyltransferase, suggesting a potential downstream effect of the drug's action. The evidence indicates that Sinocalycanchinensin G may influence the activity of these targets, which are subsequently involved in the regulation of Protein-L-isoaspartate O-methyltransferase. The integration of these pathways implies that Sinocalycanchinensin G could modulate the function of this enzyme through indirect mechanisms, possibly by affecting the activity of its upstream targets. The presence of multiple distinct targets, each with its own downstream pathway, supports the idea that the drug's effect is mediated through a network of interconnected molecular interactions, which may collectively influence the enzyme's activity.",
